Root cause: Focus not moved to close button when drawer opens because the Drawer component does not manage focus upon opening; relying on native dialog focus behavior which didn't move focus in this context.

Repair strategy: Add a listener for the 'shown.bs.drawer' event to explicitly focus the close button (#filters-close) when the drawer is shown, and clean up the listener on dispose.

Expected accessibility effect: When opening the filters drawer via keyboard, focus will move to the close button, allowing users to navigate to filter controls and apply changes without a pointer.

Functional risks: Potential conflict if other scripts also focus elements on shown event; but using specific ID reduces risk. Also ensure listener does not cause focus loops.

